    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0247" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89Belgium/44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-07T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1925—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Your 72, June 7, 3 p.m. Department has just given to the press information
                    that Belgian Government will send mission in <pb facs="0248" n="122"
                        xml:id="pg122"/> July to take up debt negotiations.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d66-f1"/> We have also informed Morgan that Department has no
                    objection to the $50,000,000 loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d66-f1" n="6" xml:id="d66-f1-content">
                <p>The Belgian commission sailed from Cherbourg, France, on July 80. For the opening
                    of negotiations, text of the agreement signed August 18, and other relevant
                    material, see <hi rendition="#italic">Combined Annual Reports of the World War
                        Foreign Debt Commission</hi>, pp. 166–182.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
